  "description": "Each case freezes the L2 header bytes, the inner bytes before auth, pair_mac = keyed BLAKE2b-128(pair key, header ‖ epk ‖ before_auth), sig (SIGNED kinds: Ed25519 over '111/msg/v1' ‖ sig_input, where sig_input = sender ‖ dest ‖ stream ‖ msg_seq ‖ kind ‖ flags ‖ frag_idx ‖ frag_count ‖ BLAKE2b-256(payload); frag fields 0 ‖ 0 when unfragmented, so a pair-key holder cannot recombine signed fragments) and the full inner (before_auth ‖ pair_mac ‖ [sig]) — the AEAD plaintext. The AEAD itself is id111's (identity/test-vectors/layer5/sealed-payload.json); epk here is a fixed value standing in for the sealer's ephemeral. pair key = BLAKE2b-256('111/pair/v1' ‖ X25519 shared ‖ sender_enc_pk ‖ recipient_enc_pk). C2 framing readings: HAS_EXT ⇒ n_ext(1) ‖ TLVs; INTRO ⇒ card_len(1) ‖ card. Every v1 packet is stream 0. 'budget' cases fill a 160/233 B bearer exactly (+1 shim byte). Rejection 'expect' tokens are the Debug form of mesh111::envelope::EnvelopeError.",
